-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg9, LAYER 1: Subchapter X, sections 271 and 272.
-- Sale, lease or exchange of assets; mortgage or pledge of assets.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the
-- Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550). It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is
-- line N of that file (an ellipsis means the line goes on).
--
-- This layer takes nobody's point of view. Each rule is the relation the text states between the
-- corporation, its stockholders or members, a secured party and a transferee, named for what it decides.
-- Sections 271, 276, 311, 312 and 313 are listed in section 114(b)(1) as sections the section 114(a)
-- reading (stockholder as member) does not touch: section 271(a) states its own rule for a nonstock
-- corporation, so its vote base is "another base named in the provision" with the text's own words.
--
-- Facts the text hands to someone else (what the board "deems expedient", whether a meeting was "duly
-- called", whether the property is "all or substantially all") are plain inputs and are never guessed.
-- Law outside the range is a plain input: Article 9 of the Uniform Commercial Code and section 1-201(b)
-- of Title 6 are not among the inputs (section 272(b)(1), (c)).

§ `Subchapter X. Sale of Assets, Dissolution and Winding Up`

§§ `s 271 Sale, lease or exchange of assets; consideration; procedure`

-- Section 271(a) names "at least 20 days' notice". A figure the text states is stated once, here.
-- src:1389 | at a meeting duly called upon at least 20 days’ notice. The notice of the meeting shall state that such a resolution will be considered.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(a) (src:1389)
`s 271(a) the least notice of the meeting` MEANS `period in days` 20

-- A majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote (a stock corporation), or of the members having
-- the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body and any other members entitled
-- to vote thereon under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws (a nonstock corporation).
-- src:1389 | adopted by the holders of a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon or, if the corporation is a nonstock corporation, by a majority of the members having the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body and any other members entitled to vote thereon under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(a) (src:1389)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A `Vote requirement`
`s 271(a) the vote that authorizes the sale, lease or exchange` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the members having the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body and any other members entitled to vote thereon under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws")
    ELSE `a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`

-- "At least 20 days' notice": the meeting is held on or after the 20th day after the day notice was given.
-- Reading taken (fork F1 in NOTES.md): the 20th day after the notice date is itself the earliest meeting day.
-- src:1389 | at a meeting duly called upon at least 20 days’ notice. The notice of the meeting shall state that such a resolution will be considered.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(a) (src:1389)
GIVEN `the date notice of the meeting was given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 271(a) the meeting is called upon at least 20 days' notice` MEANS
    `the date of the meeting` AT LEAST (`the date` `s 271(a) the least notice of the meeting` `after` `the date notice of the meeting was given`)

-- The whole of the authorization: the board has acted at a meeting, the resolution carries, the meeting is
-- duly called upon at least 20 days' notice, and the notice states that the resolution will be considered.
-- "Duly called" is the law of sections 211 and 222 (out of range: sections 211 and 222, pieces dg4 and dg5).
-- The counts are votes (section 212(a), out of range: piece dg4); an impossible count answers NOTHING.
-- src:1389 | Every corporation may at any meeting of its board of directors or governing body sell, lease or exchange all or substantially all of its property and assets, including its goodwill and its corporate franchises, upon such terms and conditions and for such consideration, which may consist in whole or in part of money or other property, including shares of stock in, and/or other securities of, any other corporation or corporations, as its board of directors or governing body deems expedient and for the best interests of the corporation, when and as authorized by a resolution adopted by the holders of a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon or, if the corporation is a nonstock corporation, by a majority of the members …
-- src:1389 | The notice of the meeting shall state that such a resolution will be considered.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(a) (src:1389)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the board of directors or governing body acted at a meeting and deems the terms and the consideration expedient and for the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes in favor of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes entitled to be cast on the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the meeting was duly called` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: sections 211 and 222 (pieces dg4 and dg5)
      `the date notice of the meeting was given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the notice stated that such a resolution will be considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271(a) the sale, lease or exchange is authorized` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`s 271(a) the vote that authorizes the sale, lease or exchange` `the kind of corporation`) `the votes in favor of the resolution` `the votes entitled to be cast on the resolution`
    WHEN JUST carried THEN
        JUST (        `the board of directors or governing body acted at a meeting and deems the terms and the consideration expedient and for the best interests of the corporation`
              AND     carried
              AND     `the meeting was duly called`
              AND     (`s 271(a) the meeting is called upon at least 20 days' notice` WITH `the date notice of the meeting was given` IS `the date notice of the meeting was given`, `the date of the meeting` IS `the date of the meeting`)
              AND     `the notice stated that such a resolution will be considered`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- "Notwithstanding authorization or consent ... the board of directors or governing body may abandon ...
-- without further action by the stockholders or members". The text speaks only of a proposal that the
-- stockholders or members have authorized or consented to; for any other proposal it says nothing here.
-- src:1390 | (b) Notwithstanding authorization or consent to a proposed sale, lease or exchange of a corporation’s property and assets by the stockholders or members, the board of directors or governing body may abandon such proposed sale, lease or exchange without further action by the stockholders or members, subject to the rights, if any, of third parties under any contract relating thereto.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(b) (src:1390)
GIVEN `the stockholders or members have authorized or consented to the proposed sale, lease or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271(b) the board or governing body may abandon the proposed sale, lease or exchange without further action by the stockholders or members` MEANS
    IF `the stockholders or members have authorized or consented to the proposed sale, lease or exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The abandonment is "subject to the rights, if any, of third parties under any contract relating thereto".
-- src:1390 | subject to the rights, if any, of third parties under any contract relating thereto.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(b) (src:1390)
GIVEN `a third party has rights under a contract relating to the proposed sale, lease or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 271(b) the third party's contract rights survive the abandonment` MEANS
    `a third party has rights under a contract relating to the proposed sale, lease or exchange`

-- "For purposes of this section only, the property and assets of the corporation include the property and
-- assets of any subsidiary of the corporation": the figure the corporation sells from is the sum.
-- src:1391 | For purposes of this section only, the property and assets of the corporation include the property and assets of any subsidiary of the corporation. As used in this subsection, “subsidiary” means any entity wholly-owned and controlled, directly or indirectly, by the corporation and includes, without limitation, corporations, partnerships, limited partnerships, limited liability partnerships, limited liability companies, and/or statutory trusts. Notwithstanding subsection (a) of this section, except to the extent the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides, no resolution by stockholders or members shall be required for a sale, lease or exchange of property and assets of the corporation to a subsidiary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(c) (src:1391)
GIVEN `the value of the property and assets of the corporation itself` IS A NUMBER
      `the values of the property and assets of each subsidiary of the corporation` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 271(c) the value of the property and assets of the corporation, counting its subsidiaries'` MEANS
    `the value of the property and assets of the corporation itself` PLUS sum `the values of the property and assets of each subsidiary of the corporation`

-- "Subsidiary" as used in subsection (c): wholly-owned and controlled, directly or indirectly, by the
-- corporation. The kinds of entity the text lists ("includes, without limitation, corporations, partnerships,
-- limited partnerships, limited liability partnerships, limited liability companies, and/or statutory
-- trusts") do not limit it, so no kind of entity is asked.
-- src:1391 | As used in this subsection, “subsidiary” means any entity wholly-owned and controlled, directly or indirectly, by the corporation and includes, without limitation, corporations, partnerships, limited partnerships, limited liability partnerships, limited liability companies, and/or statutory trusts. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(c) (src:1391)
GIVEN `the entity is wholly-owned by the corporation, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is controlled by the corporation, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 271(c) the entity is a subsidiary of the corporation` MEANS
        `the entity is wholly-owned by the corporation, directly or indirectly`
    AND `the entity is controlled by the corporation, directly or indirectly`

-- Does section 271(a) require a resolution of the stockholders or members? Only for all or substantially all
-- of the property and assets (counting the subsidiaries'), and not for a sale, lease or exchange to a
-- subsidiary "except to the extent the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides". A provision in the
-- bylaws or in a board resolution does not displace the rule: the text names only the certificate.
-- src:1389 | sell, lease or exchange all or substantially all of its property and assets, including its goodwill and its corporate franchises, upon such terms and conditions and for such consideration, which may consist in whole or in part of money or other property, including shares of stock in, and/or other securities of, any other corporation or corporations, as its board of directors or governing body deems expedient and for the best interests of the corporation, when and as authorized by a resolution adopted by the holders of a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon or, if the corporation is a nonstock corporation, by a majority of the members having the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body and any other members entitled to vote thereon under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation, at a meeting duly called upon at least 20 days’ notice. The notice of the meeting shall state that such a resolution will be considered.
-- src:1391 | Notwithstanding subsection (a) of this section, except to the extent the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides, no resolution by stockholders or members shall be required for a sale, lease or exchange of property and assets of the corporation to a subsidiary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(a) (src:1389), (c) (src:1391)
GIVEN `the sale, lease or exchange covers all or substantially all of the property and assets of the corporation, counting those of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee is a subsidiary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where a provision requiring a resolution for a sale, lease or exchange to a subsidiary is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 271(a) and (c) a resolution of the stockholders or members is required for the sale, lease or exchange` MEANS
        `the sale, lease or exchange covers all or substantially all of the property and assets of the corporation, counting those of its subsidiaries`
    AND (      NOT `the transferee is a subsidiary of the corporation`
         OR    (CONSIDER `where a provision requiring a resolution for a sale, lease or exchange to a subsidiary is made`
                WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE))

§§ `s 272 Mortgage or pledge of assets`

-- "The authorization or consent of stockholders to the mortgage or pledge of a corporation's property and
-- assets shall not be necessary, except to the extent that the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides."
-- src:1395 | (a) The authorization or consent of stockholders to the mortgage or pledge of a corporation’s property and assets shall not be necessary, except to the extent that the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(a) (src:1395)
GIVEN `where a provision requiring the authorization or consent of stockholders to a mortgage or pledge is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 272(a) the authorization or consent of stockholders to the mortgage or pledge is necessary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where a provision requiring the authorization or consent of stockholders to a mortgage or pledge is made`
    WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Section 272(b)(2): the board authorizes an alternative sale, lease or exchange (in lieu of the secured party
-- exercising its rights) that reduces or eliminates the liabilities secured by the property, provided that
-- (i) the value is less than or equal to the liabilities being eliminated or reduced (the boundary is inside)
-- and (ii) the transaction is not prohibited by the law governing the mortgage or pledge.
-- src:1398 | the board of directors of the corporation authorizes an alternative sale, lease or exchange of such property or assets, whether with the secured party or with another person, that results in the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by such property or assets, provided that (i) the value of such property or assets is less than or equal to the total amount of such liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced and (ii) such sale, lease or exchange is not prohibited by the law governing such mortgage or pledge. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(b)(2) (src:1398)
GIVEN `the board of directors authorizes an alternative sale, lease or exchange, whether with the secured party or with another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alternative sale, lease or exchange results in the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by the property or assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the property or assets` IS A NUMBER
      `the total amount of the liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced` IS A NUMBER
      `the sale, lease or exchange is prohibited by the law governing the mortgage or pledge` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Article 9 of the Uniform Commercial Code and other law (Title 6 is not among the inputs)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 272(b)(2) the board's alternative sale, lease or exchange qualifies` MEANS
        `the board of directors authorizes an alternative sale, lease or exchange, whether with the secured party or with another person`
    AND `the alternative sale, lease or exchange results in the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by the property or assets`
    AND `the value of the property or assets` AT MOST `the total amount of the liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced`
    AND NOT `the sale, lease or exchange is prohibited by the law governing the mortgage or pledge`

-- "The provision of consideration to the corporation or to its stockholders shall not create a presumption
-- that the value of such property or assets is greater than the total amount of such liabilities": a
-- definition carrier, not a boolean, because the sentence blocks an inference and states no fact.
-- src:1398 | The provision of consideration to the corporation or to its stockholders shall not create a presumption that the value of such property or assets is greater than the total amount of such liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(b)(2) (src:1398)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 272(b)(2) the framing of consideration provided to the corporation or its stockholders` MEANS
        "The provision of consideration to the corporation or to its stockholders shall not create a presumption that the value of such property or assets is greater than the total amount of such liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced."
    ... TRUE

-- "No resolution by stockholders shall be required by section 271(a) ... if such property or assets are
-- collateral that secures a mortgage or are pledged to a secured party and either: (1) ... (2) ...".
-- Paragraph (b)(1) is the secured party's exercise of its rights without the corporation's consent
-- (Article 9 of the Uniform Commercial Code, a real property law or other law: out of range).
-- src:1396 | no resolution by stockholders shall be required by § 271(a) of this title for a sale, lease or exchange of property or assets if such property or assets are collateral that secures a mortgage or are pledged to a secured party and either:
-- src:1397 | The secured party exercises its rights under the law governing such mortgage or pledge or other applicable law, whether under Article 9 of a Uniform Commercial Code [§ 9-101 et seq. of Title 6], a real property law or other law, to effect such sale, lease or exchange without the consent of the corporation; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(b) (src:1396-1397)
GIVEN `the property or assets are collateral that secures a mortgage or are pledged to a secured party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the secured party exercises its rights under the law governing the mortgage or pledge to effect the sale, lease or exchange without the consent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Article 9 of the Uniform Commercial Code and other law
      `the board's alternative sale, lease or exchange qualifies under s 272(b)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 272(b) no resolution by stockholders is required by s 271(a) for the sale, lease or exchange of the collateral` MEANS
        `the property or assets are collateral that secures a mortgage or are pledged to a secured party`
    AND (    `the secured party exercises its rights under the law governing the mortgage or pledge to effect the sale, lease or exchange without the consent of the corporation`
         OR  `the board's alternative sale, lease or exchange qualifies under s 272(b)(2)`)

-- Section 272(c), first sentence: a failure to satisfy the proviso in (b)(2)(i) does not invalidate the sale,
-- lease or exchange if the transferee provided value (which may include the reduction or elimination of the
-- liabilities secured) and acted in good faith (as defined in section 1-201(b) of Title 6, out of range). The
-- second sentence withholds that protection from a proceeding to enjoin the transaction before consummation.
-- FALSE says only that this protection does not apply: the text does not say the transaction is then invalid.
-- src:1399 | A failure to satisfy the proviso in paragraph (b)(2)(i) of this section shall not result in the invalidation of a sale, lease or exchange if the transferee of the property or assets provided value therefor (which may include the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by such property or assets) and acted in “good-faith” (as defined in § 1-201(b) of Title 6). …
-- src:1399 | The preceding sentence shall not apply to a proceeding against the corporation and any other necessary parties to enjoin such sale, lease or exchange before the consummation thereof and shall not eliminate any liability for monetary damages for any claim, including a claim in the right of the corporation, based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(c) (src:1399)
GIVEN `the transferee provided value for the property or assets, which may include the reduction or elimination of the liabilities or obligations secured by them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee acted in good faith as defined in § 1-201(b) of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Title 6 is not among the inputs
      `the proceeding is one against the corporation and any other necessary parties to enjoin the sale, lease or exchange before its consummation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 272(c) the failure to satisfy the proviso in s 272(b)(2)(i) does not invalidate the sale, lease or exchange` MEANS
        `the transferee provided value for the property or assets, which may include the reduction or elimination of the liabilities or obligations secured by them`
    AND `the transferee acted in good faith as defined in § 1-201(b) of Title 6`
    AND (NOT `the proceeding is one against the corporation and any other necessary parties to enjoin the sale, lease or exchange before its consummation`)

-- Section 272(c), last words: the sentence "shall not eliminate any liability for monetary damages for any
-- claim, including a claim in the right of the corporation, based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a
-- current or former director or officer or stockholder". For any other claim the text says nothing.
-- src:1399 | shall not eliminate any liability for monetary damages for any claim, including a claim in the right of the corporation, based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(c) (src:1399)
GIVEN `the claim is based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(c) liability for monetary damages for the claim is not eliminated by the protection of the transferee` MEANS
    IF `the claim is based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 272(d) applies "only to certificate of incorporation provisions that first become effective on or
-- after August 1, 2023". The date is data.
-- src:1400 | provided that this subsection (d) shall apply only to certificate of incorporation provisions that first become effective on or after August 1, 2023.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(d) (src:1400)
`s 272(d) the first day of the provisions to which subsection (d) applies` MEANS YMD 2023 8 1

-- A certificate provision requiring the authorization or consent of stockholders for a sale, lease or
-- exchange "shall not apply to a transaction permitted by subsection (b) of this section unless such provision
-- expressly so requires". For a provision that first became effective before 1 August 2023 subsection (d)
-- says nothing, so the answer is NOTHING (not covered).
-- src:1400 | A provision of the certificate of incorporation that requires the authorization or consent of stockholders for a sale, lease or exchange of property or assets shall not apply to a transaction permitted by subsection (b) of this section unless such provision expressly so requires; provided that this subsection (d) shall apply only to certificate of incorporation provisions that first become effective on or after August 1, 2023.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(d) (src:1400)
GIVEN `the date the certificate provision first became effective` IS A DATE
      `the certificate provision expressly requires its application to a transaction permitted by s 272(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(d) the certificate provision requiring stockholder authorization or consent applies to the transaction permitted by s 272(b)` MEANS
    IF `the date the certificate provision first became effective` AT LEAST `s 272(d) the first day of the provisions to which subsection (d) applies`
    THEN JUST `the certificate provision expressly requires its application to a transaction permitted by s 272(b)`
    ELSE NOTHING
